Package: soilsampling
Type: Package
Title: Design and Optimization of Soil Sampling Schemes
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: c(
        person(
            given = "Carlos",
            family = "Carbajal",
            email = "ccarbajal@educagis.com",
            role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Provides methods for designing and optimizing soil sampling
        schemes. Available designs include simple random sampling, stratified
        random sampling, spatial coverage sampling from compact geographical
        strata built by k-means clustering, composite sampling, and maxvol
        optimal design, which applies a D-optimal maximum volume criterion to
        select samples in feature space. Optimization tools choose a
        conditioned Latin hypercube sample size from Kullback-Leibler
        divergence, refine an existing design by simulated annealing against a
        random forest objective, and identify environmentally similar
        replacements for inaccessible sites. Validation metrics assess
        stratification quality through coverage efficiency and distance
        statistics. Methods follow Walvoort, Brus and de Gruijter (2010)
        <doi:10.1016/j.cageo.2010.04.005>, Petrovskaia, Korveh and Maas (2021)
        <doi:10.1016/j.geoderma.2020.114733>, Malone, Minasny and Brungard
        (2019) <doi:10.7717/peerj.6451>, and Wadoux, Brus and Heuvelink (2019)
        <doi:10.1016/j.geoderma.2019.113913>.
